Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Local monodromies from the transformed residues", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"c1dcebb1-3efd-44ca-b770-86c5fff714a2"],

Cell["\<\
For a normalized Fuchsian system, a local fundamental matrix has the form \
H_p(t)t^R_p with H_p(0)=I, so a positive loop in t gives exp(2 Pi I R_p). At \
infinity t=1/tau. The minimal-polynomial identities below reduce these \
exponentials without diagonalization. They use zeta=Exp[I Pi d], so Exp[2 Pi \
I eps]=1/zeta and Exp[2 Pi I(d-11/2)]=-zeta^2.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"761d6e3f-db3c-491c-a27a-332846c132c5"],

