Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Derived orbit-basis matrices", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"426cec0b-6b19-4f96-8b81-3c16e77cd5b2"],

Cell["\<\
At a matching point, U[right,left] = F_right^-1 F_left. The products uh, um \
and ui therefore give F_0 = F_p U_p. Consequently M_p = U_p^-1 L_p U_p acts \
in the zero-centered basis. With C=(vStar,M_H vStar,M_minusOne vStar), the \
final generators are rho_p=C^-1 M_p C. The next output is computed from these \
transported matrices, not copied from predefined rho formulas. Infinity uses \
its own positive-real matching chain; no product identity is used to \
determine it.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"be32e9b9-f9b5-42f7-87ca-f2291f6b3579"],

